{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468867-planetary-s-bleed-as-trinity-continuum-background","id":1468867,"title":"Planetary's \"Bleed\" as Trinity Continuum Background","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-25T13:06:09-08:00","id":1468867,"title":"Planetary's \"Bleed\" as Trinity Continuum Background","content":"The basic idea is to adopt something largely like the &quot;Bleed&quot; from &quot;Planetary&quot; comics as a background idea for the Trinity Continuum. As Warren Ellis got the ideas for the Bleed and Holographic reality from real-world theories about the nature of reality (yes these theories are pseudoscience, pseudoscience gets used a lot in Sci Fi and comics) this won't can't involve copyright infringement.<br /> <br /> The Bleed, simply put, is a para spatial realm between realities. Star Trek called it the Corridors Between the Universes, Doctor Who called it The Howling Halls. The Doctor Who episode &quot;The Warrior's Gate&quot; took place in a version of this, as did the earlier episode &quot;The Mind Robber.&quot; The Bleed is connected to the idea that actual reality is two-dimensional. The three dimensional reality that we experience is a Hologram. This means we and everything we experience are information. Change the information and change reality.<br /> <br /> The advantage of this idea for this game setting is this it A) gives flux a useful Pseudoscience rational, B) it allows &quot;magic&quot; as a &quot;cheat code&quot; for reality. This means Flux powers and Essence/Magick can be different forms of the same thing. This also gives a justification for a vast but finite number of parallel worlds in a stable pattern, Ellis had his characters call it the &quot;Snowflake&quot; and said it was arrayed in a 196,833 dimensional space.<br /> <br /> This allows multiple campaigns to take place on nearby parallel worlds. Heck the Classic and New Worlds of Darkness could be out there.<br /> <br /> Thus if you wanted a fairly close to the Metaplot world to interact with a world where the Telluric energies of Adventure! never faded, and the 21st century is a Raygun Gothic wonderland, it works. If you want to have the New World Order taking over the Aeon Society while the Hermetics try to get Divis Mal to both grow up and ally with them, that also works. <br /> <br /> Reactions? Refinements? .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T13:13:43-08:00","id":1468868,"title":"","content":"<b>In Media Res</b> already has something like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T23:03:17-08:00","id":1468895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468867-planetary-s-bleed-as-trinity-continuum-background?p=1468868#post1468868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>In Media Res</b> already has something like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where? I'm rereading In Media Res but I can't seem to find it.<br /> <br /> In response to Astromancer we actually use the Bleed in our game as an explanation for Telluric energy and the Hammersmith explosion. Basically Hammersmith tried to tap the Bleed for energy and did the equivalent of hooking a AAA battery to a power plant and being surprised when it overloaded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T01:14:53-08:00","id":1468907,"title":"","content":"The name in TC for the Bleed is The Myst. I don\u2019t have the book here, but it is described in the story about a Heist of Le Fantomes (if I am not wrong).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T04:29:25-08:00","id":1468912,"title":"","content":"Found it. Page 35 from In Media Res in a sidebar. Its sorta like a half step into the Bleed. I'm curious if there is any connection to the Shadow that they talked about in the Assassins preview. Its not quite the same as the Shadow is described more as a perception filter but as both seem to be Flux effects it could be that the Mist is a more powerful form of the Shadow, maybe with the ultimate form being Max's power? Or to bring it back to the opening topic opening gateways to the Bleed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T17:56:09-08:00","id":1469606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarrenDalca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468867-planetary-s-bleed-as-trinity-continuum-background?p=1468912#post1468912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Found it. Page 35 from In Media Res in a sidebar. Its sorta like a half step into the Bleed. I'm curious if there is any connection to the Shadow that they talked about in the Assassins preview. Its not quite the same as the Shadow is described more as a perception filter but as both seem to be Flux effects it could be that the Mist is a more powerful form of the Shadow, maybe with the ultimate form being Max's power? Or to bring it back to the opening topic opening gateways to the Bleed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Myst and the Shadow are not even close to the same thing. The Myst is an extra-dimensional space that can allow access to parallel worlds/universes. Want to bring your Nova characters and Psion characters together? You go through the Myst, having one set visit the other set.<br /> <br /> The Shadow, meanwhile, is more of a Flux-fortified social barrier/perceptual filter. Did you ever watch the <i>Free Guy </i>movie with Ryan Reynolds? Remember the bit where he got the glasses that let him see contracts, power-ups and the like? Basically, in Assassins, the only ones who have the special &quot;glasses&quot; are the Assassins. Not even Talents, Psiads or Novas have access to the Shadow. Unless, y'know, they do, because some Assassinish person allowed them to for whatever reason.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T05:43:14-08:00","id":1469642,"title":"","content":"Shadow is based on Flux, which is defined in the Core book on page 17 as the energy's of two worlds colliding.<br /> And Talents use of Flux is talked about as changing probabilities or replacing snippets of this world with that of another one in the Continuum, especially when they use Dramatic Editing. <br /> <br /> So the perception filter that Shadow grants (to me at least, your game your rules) would be influencing the probability of anyone ever looking closer. They still see the building and know its there but they never go beyond that due to Flux influencing the chances that it never happens.<br /> <br /> The way the Mist was described (once again, to me) had that same vibe. You can't pass through solid objects that don't move but if they move often like a door or gate you can push through them. No real explanation is given as to why, but to me that says that you are using the Mist to find the probabilities where the thing isn't in your way. So in my games Both Mist and Shadow are just different applications of Talents manipulating The Bleed (Flux). One as a unconscious effect based on Inspiration one as a conscious effort through Super Science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T12:17:18-08:00","id":1469658,"title":"","content":"My basic idea is that nearby (for a given value and definition of nearby) parallel worlds makes a great addition to the setting. Picture this set up, Earth Alpha (your campaign setting), Earth Beta (the basic metaplot setting), Earth Gamma (an actual superheroes setting {Novas aren't supers}), Earth Delta (some variation of the WoD), Earth Epsilon (an Scions setting), Earth Zeta (a world were the British Empire rules just like it did in the late 19th century, but with neither America nor Germany as viable rivals, it's Novas are rivals and often foes to our world's Novas), Earth Eta (a world were France won the War of Spanish Succession and rules with an Iron Fist, their Novas would be honorable foes of our world's Novas), Earth Theta ( a world were the Assyrian Empire rules to this day, their Novas would be dishonorable foes), Earth Iota (a world built on Sword and Sorcery &amp; Sword and Planet tropes, inspired/Adventure! type campaigns in a setting like the pre- classical world), Earth Kappa ( a world were the Greeks applied their genius to practical problems and had the scientific and industrial revolutions in ancient times, Novas in a far future setting), [I'll do the rest of the alphabet later].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 12-05-2021, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T13:41:44-08:00","id":1469763,"title":"","content":"Earth Lambda (the creatures of the WoD coexist with inspired, Talents, and Psiads) Earth Mu (this world is going through the later decades of the sixteenth century, inspired swordsmen and alchemists adventure in this Elizabethan England), Earth Nu (Inspired Wuxia in late Qing China), Earth Xi (Novas show up without Inspired coming before them in WWII), Earth Omicron (Zombie apocalypse), Earth Pi (utopian society, crystal spires and togas type), Earth Rho (a late 21st century Nova setting with Anima style tech and lots of space colonisation), Earth Sigma ( an inspired Space Opera setting, no Psions, Psiads, or Novas, but plenty of two-fisted action), Earth Tau (King Arthur is returning to England after an apocalypse, inspired knights and mutants, the Gravitational Realignment Anti Inertial Link might be important.), Earth Upsilon (the Scions of the Gods show up at the same time as Novas. Is this a good thing?). [I'll do the rest of the alphabet later].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 12-06-2021, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T15:42:01-08:00","id":1469773,"title":"","content":"Earth Chi (this world has Novas, Talents, Psiad/Psions with the versatility of the first and the power of the second, but none of this world's cultures seem to have any relationship the the PC's Earth. Their cultural values and moral perspective are wildly different than the PC's), Earth Phi (This Earth has been conquered by an alien empire with its own Novas), Earth Psi (this Earth is going through the year 5421AD, they have no flux related individuals, not even Talents, and they are intensely interested in such powers), Earth Omega ( this Earth is the home of a race of Paranoid Posthumans. They have vast and amazingly flexible powers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}